## 15.2 Ownership and dependency rules

1. CORE-001 through CORE-008 remain the canonical owners of their existing business domains.
2. AI-001 remains the canonical owner of the existing AI platform.
3. The Fastify application is an API and orchestration boundary; it must not become a second business-domain engine.
4. The Python runtime is a private integration boundary for existing Python domain capabilities.
5. PostgreSQL is the authoritative persistent business store according to the approved schema.
6. Redis is ephemeral coordination/cache, not a replacement business ledger.
7. Kafka transports durable events; it does not become another source of business truth.
8. Temporal owns durable long-running workflow orchestration; do not introduce a competing workflow engine.
9. Qdrant and search projections are derived and rebuildable.
10. ACRL remains continuity, reconstruction and recovery infrastructure, not a customer-facing business runtime.
11. Frontend code consumes backend-owned contracts; it must not own backend authorization or business rules.
12. No new CORE domain, parallel identity system, event system, financial ledger, AI gateway, history store or evidence engine may be introduced without an approved ownership decision.

